@title a short name for somebody you name often

A nickname is your own abbreviation for another person's name.
Nobody else sees it: it is there so you type less. The verbs are
not translated yet:

  apodo <nickname> <name>   creates it, or changes one you had.
  apodo <nickname>          says what name it stands for.
  apodo                     lists every one you have.
  quitarapodo <nickname>    deletes it.

'nick' and 'apodos' do the same as 'apodo'; 'dnick' does the same
as 'quitarapodo'.

Wherever somebody's name is expected, the nickname works just as
well: after "apodo g Guardia", "tell g hello" talks to Guardia.
